X:7
T:Lalishrita
T:Tamil lullaby, from a phonogram (sketch)
C:traditional (Tamil Nadu)
O:India, Tamil Nadu (Srirangam)
R:lullaby
S:Fox Strangways, The Music of Hindostan (1914), Ex. 155, p. 64
N:A SKETCH of the first two lines: Adagio, crotchet 70, taken from a phonogram, so the book's notation has triplets and grace notes; the words are Fox Strangways's singing version. The melody circles G with E below and C above. Every bar wants checking against the plate; the third and fourth lines (I bring thee sleep; On the wings of my melodies) are not read yet.
M:6/8
L:1/8
Q:1/4=70
K:C
%%style drone
C | C G G G2 G/A/ | G/E/G/E/ (3G/E/G/ G E z G | G c c B3/2 A/2 B | d3/2 c/2 B A G (3G/E/G/ | G2 z E G |]
w: Ba__ by mine, light_ of____ my eyes, Here in thy cra__-dle bright__ with flowers Through
N:2: Srirangam island rises fair Where Kaveris meet; I lay thee there at Sriranga raja's feet, Full sure of His tender care.
N:3: The golden nails no longer move On the divided cradle swung; The song is sung; my ship is borne Safe home, my babe, on the ocean of love.
